course: dictionary
lesson: 5511
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear many coats. Lead is one spelling with several meanings, and two different sounds. When it means to guide or to be in charge, say it «leed». When it means the soft grey metal, say it «led».
explain: Look at the words around lead to find its meaning. «Our team leads by two goals» means they are winning, because leads is followed by a score. «This path leads to the beach» means the path goes to the beach. Ask yourself: what would fit here?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you think lead means «go in front» in «bright beach lights can lead hatchlings the wrong way», the sentence still makes sense: the lights guide the baby turtles, but in the wrong direction.
fact: Lead (leed) can be a verb: to go in front and show the way, or to be winning.
fact: «This path leads to the beach» means the path goes to the beach.
fact: A lead (leed) is a strap for a dog, or a wire for electricity. In America, a dog's lead is called a leash.
fact: Lead (led) is a soft, heavy, grey metal, and it is poisonous if swallowed.
fact: Pencil «lead» (led) is really graphite, not the metal.
exercise: «Peel back the husk and each long silky thread leads to one kernel.» What does leads mean here? | Breaks into pieces | Sings loudly | *Goes to, reaches | Is the heaviest part
exercise: «Our team leads by two goals.» What does leads mean here? | Is at the back, losing badly | Gives two presents | *Is winning, ahead of the other team | Is wearing a red shirt
exercise: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, hot enough to melt lead.» Say the word «led». In this sentence, what is lead? | *The soft, heavy grey metal | To go in front and show the way | A strap for a dog | First place in a race
test: Keep your dog on a lead near busy roads. What is a lead here? | To go in front of the dog | The main actor in a play | *A strap for a dog | A wire for electricity in the wall
test: «A slippery slope says one small step will lead to disaster.» What does lead to mean here? | To melt into a liquid | *To cause it, or end up at it | To be winning the race | To guide someone safely home
exam: «Warmer sand gives more girl hatchlings, and bright beach lights can lead hatchlings the wrong way.» What does lead mean in this sentence? | Is a soft grey metal | *Guides, shows the way | Is winning | Is a dog strap
